%n melemmū | ih[a]lliqū-ma | namrīrū | irrupū | ana erpi
#note: See @bib{RN117@263–264}: “Or, reading @i{irrubū}, 'entering’ [instead of ‘fading’]. The masculine counterpart of the common @i{erpetu} otherwise appears only in @i{MSL} IV, p. 38, Emesal Voc. III 119–22, as a counterpart of @sux{dungu}, ‘cloud’.”
// cf. L I.4 OB "Schøyen₃" b+4'

%n kīma (|) watmū | irtanappudū | iq-qīšim
#note: See @bib{RN117@264}: “Although the scribe uses an apocopated preposition nowhere else, the writing @i{i-qí-ši-im} probably represents @i{iq-qīšim}. Bauer’s reading @i{di-ši-im}, ‘spring grass’, is not impossible.”
// cf. L I.4 MB "Boğ₁" a+5'

